open scoped ENNReal NNReal BigOperators

abbrev YuiEucl (n : ℕ) := EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)
def YuiI : Set ℝ := Set.Icc 0 1
def YuiSnoc {n : ℕ} (x : YuiEucl n) (t : ℝ) : YuiEucl (n + 1) :=
  WithLp.toLp 2 (Fin.snoc (fun i => x i) t)
def YuiHead {n : ℕ} (z : YuiEucl (n + 1)) : YuiEucl n :=
  WithLp.toLp 2 (fun i : Fin n => z i.castSucc)
def YuiLast {n : ℕ} (z : YuiEucl (n + 1)) : ℝ := z (Fin.last n)
def YuiCylinder {n : ℕ} (E : Set (YuiEucl n)) : Set (YuiEucl (n + 1)) :=
  {z | YuiHead z ∈ E ∧ YuiLast z ∈ YuiI}
noncomputable def YuiCost {X : Type*} [PseudoEMetricSpace X] {ι : Type*}
    (s : ℝ) (U : ι → Set X) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  ∑' i, ⨆ (_ : (U i).Nonempty), (Metric.ediam (U i)) ^ s
def YuiCover {X : Type*} [PseudoEMetricSpace X] (δ : ℝ) (A : Set X)
    (U : ℕ → Set X) : Prop :=
  A ⊆ ⋃ i, U i ∧ ∀ i, Metric.ediam (U i) ≤ ENNReal.ofReal δ
noncomputable def YuiContent {X : Type*} [PseudoEMetricSpace X]
    (s δ : ℝ) (A : Set X) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  ⨅ (U : ℕ → Set X) (_ : YuiCover δ A U), YuiCost s U
noncomputable def YuiMeasure {X : Type*} [PseudoEMetricSpace X]
    (s : ℝ) (A : Set X) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  ⨆ (δ : ℝ) (_ : 0 < δ), YuiContent s δ A
", "parameters": [{"name": "n", "type": "ℕ"}, {"name": "E", "type": "Set (YuiEucl n)"}], "representation": "Use EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)=PiLp 2 (constant ℝ), indexed by Fin n, with its native L2 metric and Borel structure; n is a natural ambient dimension including 0. YuiSnoc appends a real coordinate and YuiHead/YuiLast recover it; YuiCylinder E is defined by these coordinates directly in EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin (n+1)). T003 checks the coordinate inverse and Euclidean distance identities used by all cylinder arguments, so there is no max-product metric or unproved metric replacement. The interval remains Set.Icc (0:ℝ) 1. Metric.ediam, YuiCost, YuiContent and YuiMeasure take values in ℝ≥0∞; ^ with a real exponent is ENNReal.rpow. The supremum over a nonempty witness equals ediam^s and over an empty witness equals zero, giving the prescribed empty-cover convention even at exponent zero. All uses of Hausdorff content or normalization are guarded by s>0 and δ>0. Cover sequences enumerate countable covers with empty padding; the positive-diameter construction uses a subset of ℕ to avoid duplicating finite nonempty families. dimH is native, defined as the supremum of nonnegative exponents with infinite native unnormalized Hausdorff measure; its nonnegative extended codomain gives dimH empty=0. Positive real exponents are embedded by ENNReal.ofReal only with the relevant positivity; D remains dimH E in ℝ≥0∞ and its toReal value is used only downstream of T005's finiteness. Nat casts of n and constants are finite ENNReal values. Lebesgue measure/integrals in the slicing and interval workers are volume on ℝ and the nonnegative lintegral. All five M facts are supplied by direct pinned Mathlib use, not additional premises. Background notes remain optional node-local references. N outputs are unchanged; auxiliary T001 exposes the uniform metric-space normalization calculation already used in S001 so both Euclidean and real-interval instances can share it.", "inputs": [{"id": "T003", "binder": "h_T003", "type": "∀ k : ℕ, (∀ (x : YuiEucl k) (t : ℝ), YuiHead (YuiSnoc x t) = x ∧ YuiLast (YuiSnoc x t) = t) ∧ (∀ z : YuiEucl (k + 1), YuiSnoc (YuiHead z) (YuiLast z) = z) ∧ (∀ (x y : YuiEucl k) (t u : ℝ), dist (YuiSnoc x t) (YuiSnoc y u) = Real.sqrt ((dist x y) ^ 2 + |t-u| ^ 2)) ∧ LipschitzWith 1 (YuiHead (n := k)) ∧ LipschitzWith 1 (YuiLast (n := k))"}, {"id": "T005", "binder": "h_T005", "type": "(0 ≤ dimH E ∧ dimH E ≤ (n : ℝ≥0∞) ∧ dimH E < ⊤) ∧ (∀ (s δ : ℝ), 0 < s → 0 < δ → YuiContent s δ E < ⊤)"}], "target": "∀ s δ : ℝ, 0 < s → 0 < δ → ∀ V : ℕ → Set (YuiEucl (n + 1)), YuiCover δ (YuiCylinder E) V → ∀ ε : ℝ, 0 < ε → YuiContent s δ E ≤ YuiCost (s + 1) V + ENNReal.ofReal ε", "explanation": "Slice integration bound for an arbitrary original cover V; V, its nonempty index subtype and its diameters do not depend on ε. By finite mesh all diameters are finite. T003 bounds head and last projections. With rho_i the real finite diameter, enlarge each last projection to the bounded open interval J_i by eta_i=ε*2^(-i-1)/(1+rho_i^s). The weighted eta-error sums to at most ε, including zero diameters. The corresponding head slices cover E at each t∈I. Integrate c≤sum rho_i^s*1_Ji over volume.restrict YuiI. Here c=YuiContent s δ E is finite by T005 and volume(I)=1. Apply MeasureTheory.lintegral_tsum at the countable nonempty index subtype with the measurable interval indicators and ENNReal coefficients; only AE measurability of each summand is needed, with no finiteness or sigma-finiteness requirement. Indicators integrate to volume(J_i∩I) and interval length bounds give cost+ε. Neither V nor its projections require measurability. Convert each finite diameter to a real only after its mesh bound; restore ENNReal powers and nonnegative series at the interface.", "source_steps": [{"id": "S016", "text": "Fix s>0 and delta>0. Take any countable family V and introduce L1: V is a delta-cover of F. Enumerate it with possible empty padding, discard empties, and write T⊆N for the remaining indices; all i-series in this inference are over T. Define rho_i=diam(V_i), and A_i and B_i as its first and last coordinate projections. By the Euclidean distance formula, each coordinate projection is 1-Lipschitz. Thus A_i and B_i are nonempty and have diameter ≤rho_i≤delta. In particular B_i is bounded, with finite infimum and supremum and sup B_i-inf B_i≤rho_i. Put c=H^s_delta(E). By N002, c is finite."}, {"id": "S017", "text": "For arbitrary epsilon>0 set eta_i=epsilon 2^(-i-1)/(1+rho_i^s)>0. By F001 define the bounded open interval J_i=(inf B_i-eta_i/2,sup B_i+eta_i/2). It contains B_i and its length is sup B_i-inf B_i+eta_i≤rho_i+eta_i. This construction also works when rho_i=0. No measurability of V_i, A_i or B_i is asserted or required. Furthermore sum_i eta_i rho_i^s≤epsilon sum_{i in T}2^(-i-1)≤epsilon, since 0≤rho_i^s/(1+rho_i^s)≤1."}, {"id": "S018", "text": "For each t∈I, the A_i with t∈J_i cover E. Indeed, for each x∈E, the point (x,t)∈F lies in some V_i, so x∈A_i and t∈B_i⊆J_i. Their diameters are ≤rho_i≤delta by F001. The definition of the infimum H^s_delta(E) therefore gives c≤sum_i rho_i^s 1_{J_i}(t). Define f_i(t)=rho_i^s 1_{J_i}(t). Each f_i is a nonnegative Borel measurable function: J_i is open and the coefficient rho_i^s is finite. Thus it is almost-everywhere measurable for lambda restricted to I."}, {"id": "S019", "text": "Integrate F003 over I, whose Lebesgue measure is one. Monotonicity of the nonnegative integral gives c≤integral_I sum_i f_i. Apply M001 on R with measure lambda restricted to I, index type T, and this f: T is countable as a subset of N, and F003 gives the required almost-everywhere measurability. We obtain c≤sum_i integral_I f_i=sum_i rho_i^s |J_i∩I|. The last equality is the integral formula for a nonnegative constant times a measurable indicator, which follows directly from the simple-function definition of the integral. By F002, c≤sum_i rho_i^s |J_i∩I|≤sum_i rho_i^(s+1)+sum_i eta_i rho_i^s≤sum_i rho_i^(s+1)+epsilon. Here rho_i^s rho_i=rho_i^(s+1) also at rho_i=0 since s>0; nonnegative series permit termwise comparison and splitting."}], "boundary": "Only listed inputs are project premises. The pinned Mathlib environment is freely available; no sibling proof is supplied.", "background_supplement_sha256": "1bf0b9c7347572e230e12960e1ad72681eb160b097abdd7fb42c849256a378a3", "objects": [], "representations": [], "bridges": [], "shared_inputs": [], "background_note_index": [{"id": "R004.BG001", "at": "/inference/argument/0/text", "kind": "mathematical", "fact": "If V is a nonempty subset of Eucl(n)×R with finite diameter rho, both coordinate projections are nonempty and have diameter at most rho. Its last-coordinate image B is bounded and has real infimum and supremum with sup B−inf B≤rho."}, {"id": "R004.BG002", "at": "/inference/argument/1/text", "kind": "mathematical", "fact": "For a nonempty bounded B⊆R of span at most rho and eta>0, J=(inf B−eta/2,sup B+eta/2) is bounded, open and contains B, with lambda(J∩I)≤rho+eta. For T⊆N and eta_i=epsilon 2^(−i−1)/(1+rho_i^s), sum_{i∈T} eta_i rho_i^s≤epsilon."}, {"id": "R004.BG003", "at": "/inference/argument/2/text", "kind": "mathematical", "fact": "For s>0, the map r↦r^s is increasing on nonnegative real numbers, has 0^s=0, and finite input gives finite output. Thus a countable delta-cover with diameters bounded by rho_i has s-cost at most sum rho_i^s. A constant nonnegative coefficient times an indicator of an open subset of R is Borel measurable and hence almost-everywhere measurable for any measure on this Borel space."}, {"id": "R004.BG004", "at": "/inference/argument/3/text", "kind": "mathematical", "fact": "For nu=lambda restricted to I, a nonnegative constant c has integral c because nu(R)=lambda(I)=1. If c≤g on I for measurable nonnegative g, then c≤integral g dnu. For a Borel J and finite a≥0, integral a 1_J dnu=a lambda(J∩I)."}, {"id": "R004.BG005", "at": "/inference/argument/3/text", "kind": "mathematical", "fa